# Local config: CuteAFD v5.0.0 (tag d8e566e8), 2x RTX PRO 6000, local experts, no Sparks. BF16-core derived checkpoint (K4-Core-K6 experts + MTP, 316 core matrices as BF16 originals), which v5 loads on the legacy fused path. As launched: the default FP8 conversions (row128 KDA, FP8 head, FP8 prefill MLA+FFN). All original precision: --set GLM5_FLASH_KDA_FP8=off --set GLM5_FLASH_FP8_HEAD=off --set GLM5_FLASH_FP8_PREFILL=off.
# Ported from the v4.0.0 file in <stacks>/cuteafd-v4/local (local settings kept: ADDR on 127.0.0.1,
# USAGE=off, MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS at the engine ceiling, image pinned by digest, drafter pinned).
# Changes from v4.0.0: COORDINATOR_GPU=0 -> COORDINATOR_GPUS=0,1 (the old key is an unknown key on v5: hard error);
# MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=0 (v5 has no fixed ceiling; <=0 means bounded only by the context left after the prompt);
# INSTANCE=local-v5 (own launcher state and container name); v5 image. Loop abort is new in v5 and left at its
# default (on): a reply it ends reports finish_reason=length with usage.finish_detail="repetition".
#
#   cd <stacks>/cuteafd-v5 && HF_HOME=<hf-home> ./run.sh --config local/glm53-flash-exl3-k4-core-k6-bf16core-2rtx.config --dry-run
